{
 "half": "SE: every ring-owned site not in half NW (NW = v < -900 or u < -900, plus the ring node nearest the dividing line on each side: the J Ave T (-800, 288.7) and the 6th St T (657.3, -800)). This half meets NW at the J Ave T's east tile edge (s_rg_b131_1, core-built) and at the 6th St T's south tile edge (s_rg_se_b140_2); the stub b095 (6th St) to that T is SE.",
 "not_served": [],
 "note": "Ring family half SE integration table (17 Nov, stage 2 site builder). pos = [u, y, v] in the GRID frame (x = u along 10th St ESE, z = v along Amber SSW, origin Amber x 10th; y = height); yaw in degrees (Godot: +z -> (sin yaw, cos yaw)). Boulevard pieces and T-junctions are authored in the grid frame about their anchor (yaw 0); stubs along +z from their lattice junction. Includes the core stage's pieces that serve SE sites (built_by). Built by tools/city/pilot/pieces/road_rg_SE.gd over road_rg.gd.",
 "overrides": {
  "250.0,345.0": "bus stops both ways at B Ave x Ocean Blvd (the library's look-back rule left 667 m without a stop between Amber's signals and W; Yasin's approved rule: stops never more than ~330 m apart). b135 and b161 are laid out with it; b161 part 2 is therefore rebuilt here (s_rg_se_b161_2) and the core's example s_rg_b161_2 is superseded (its file is untouched, it is not in this table)",
  "b130": "11th St, B Ave -> W: the library's stub plan has no far T (W is a locked sample), built by road_rg_SE._build_b130: std section from j_rs_2l2r_opp_a's east tile edge 20 to W's west leg end (s_wfd, 100 m from W: z 220), the whole -4.65 m rise (6.0 -> W's pad 1.35, ROADKIT_SPEC 6) on one smoothstep, max 3.5 %, the eastbound far-side bus stop after B Ave",
  "stub starts": "measured 20.0 on every resstd junction (res section) and 17.5 on j_am_11th (hs): the library's SEC z0, no change"
